/*!
  \page example_cxx_basic_page Sphere fitting and GLS on the CPU

  This example fits algebraic spheres on a random noisy unit sphere, at the position of its first point, with several
  methods:
  - Ponca::OrientedSphereFit (APSS), with the Growing Least Squares parameters (Ponca::GLSParam),
  - Ponca::UnorientedSphereFit, which ignores the orientation of the normals,
  - Ponca::OrientedSphereFit with space derivatives (Ponca::BasketDiff), which also provides principal curvatures,
  - Ponca::SphereFit, which only uses the positions.

  The neighbors are collected with a Ponca::KdTreeDense, and added one by one to the fits (`init`, `addNeighbor`,
  `finalize`). For each method, the program prints the center and radius of the sphere, the value and gradient of the
  scalar field, the GLS parameters and the projection of the evaluation position.

  Build and run:
  \code{.sh}
  cmake --build build --target ponca_basic_cpu
  ./build/examples/cpp/ponca_basic_cpu
  \endcode

  See also \ref fitting_firstSteps and \ref fitting_derivatives.

  \include cpp/ponca_basic_cpu.cpp
*/
